README.md
# docker-compose.yml and deploy/ are deliberately NOT ignored, despite being
# deployment config rather than application content. The backend-test stage
# asserts things about them — that no host port is published, that Caddy is not
# configured to trust the whole internet — and those assertions are what make
# `client_ip()` safe to believe. Excluded from the context, they skipped
# silently in CI and ran only on a developer's machine, which is the "control
# that fails open" case in AGENTS.md.
#
# Nothing is baked into the shipped image: the stage that reads them is
# discarded, and the final stage copies only /tests-passed out of it.
